  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 5♣. After ruffing the opening heart lead, South's only possible losers are in spades. If trumps break 2-1, South can play to guarantee only 2 spade losers no matter how the defenders' spades are distributed.\n\nSouth draws 2 rounds of trump. He crosses to the dummy in diamonds and leads a heart, ruffing in the closed hand. Another diamond is played to dummy and another heart is ruffed.\n\nThe ♦A is cashed to discard dummy's last heart, eliminating hearts and diamonds at the same time. South leads a spade. Whatever West follows with, dummy covers as cheaply as possible. East can win the trick, but he will be endplayed. East must either set up a spade trick for North or provide a ruff and discard.\n\nThe North-South spade combination is certain to produce one trick in a elimination position, regardless of how the East-West spades are distributed.",
